<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Workbench: Privacy Preferences Policy Control (PPPC) profile for IT administrators.

  Covers both editions, signed by Developer ID team GHVAAH9P5Z:
    Workbench          com.ethdawg.workbench
    Workbench Preview  com.ethdawg.workbench.preview   (testing edition; delete its entries if you only deploy Workbench)

  Deliver it through your MDM to the DEVICE channel. It takes effect only when delivered by MDM; a
  copy installed by hand won't grant anything. Apple requires user-approved MDM, and Apple's
  deployment guide also says supervision. On macOS 14-26.1 the approvals it grants don't appear in
  Privacy & Security's lists (from 26.2 they may); the device-management profile's details in System
  Settings always list them.

  What this grants:
    Accessibility              Allow. Automatic paste reads the focused text field and confirms the paste.
    PostEvent                  Allow. Automatic paste sends Command-V to the app you are typing in.
    ScreenCapture              AllowStandardUserToSetSystemService. Snap and Snap & Talk. Apple does not
                               let a profile switch this on. This value lets a standard (non-admin)
                               user switch it on in System Settings without an administrator.
    SystemPolicyDesktopFolder  Allow. Used only by "Import Desktop screenshots". Optional: delete it and
                               macOS asks the user the first time instead. A standard user can answer.

  Deliberately left out:
    Microphone, Camera   In PPPC these keys can only Deny. Users allow them in macOS's own prompt
                         the first time they dictate or turn on a camera. A standard user normally
                         allows them there. On macOS 27 (supervised), the declarative App Settings Privacy
                         PermissionDefaults can suggest Allow instead; the person accepts it once.
    System audio         Meetings records the other side of a call through Core Audio process taps
                         (TCC service kTCCServiceAudioCapture). PPPC has no key for it, and macOS 26
                         does not accept it in a profile. The user allows it in macOS's prompt the
                         first time Meetings records a call.
    ListenEvent          Workbench does not use Input Monitoring. Its keyboard monitors only run with
                         Accessibility approval, which is covered above.
    AppleEvents, SpeechRecognition, Full Disk Access   Not used.

  macOS 26.2 deprecated granting Accessibility by profile. Apple's 27.0 reference says the grant still
  applies on macOS 27, with a notification, and the user can turn it off. During the 27 betas, Apple
  DTS said the ability is removed, and testers saw it ignored unless PostEvent was also in the payload.
  Test on a macOS 27 Mac before relying on it, and keep PostEvent here: the declarative replacement
  (com.apple.configuration.app.settings Privacy, supervised Macs only) has no PostEvent key. Check
  that your MDM supports that declaration type before relying on it.

  CodeRequirement values come from `codesign -dr -` on the shipping apps. They pin bundle ID, Apple's
  Developer ID chain and team GHVAAH9P5Z, so they survive updates and certificate renewals. They do
  not match ad hoc (locally built) copies.

  Replace PayloadIdentifier / PayloadOrganization / PayloadUUID values with your own if your MDM does
  not regenerate them.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>PayloadContent</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>PayloadDescription</key>
			<string>Lets Workbench paste dictated text for you, and lets standard users allow Screen Recording for Snap.</string>
			<key>PayloadDisplayName</key>
			<string>Workbench privacy permissions</string>
			<key>PayloadIdentifier</key>
			<string>com.ethdawg.workbench.it.pppc.tcc</string>
			<key>PayloadOrganization</key>
			<string>REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-ORGANISATION</string>
			<key>PayloadType</key>
			<string>com.apple.TCC.configuration-profile-policy</string>
			<key>PayloadUUID</key>
			<string>D99B6E1C-F84D-4E6F-B134-273631BDE9B4</string>
			<key>PayloadVersion</key>
			<integer>1</integer>
			<key>Services</key>
			<dict>
				<key>Accessibility</key>
				<array>
					<dict>
						<key>Authorization</key>
						<string>Allow</string>
						<key>CodeRequirement</key>
						<string>identifier "com.ethdawg.workbench" and anchor apple generic and certificate 1[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.2.6] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.1.13] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = GHVAAH9P5Z</string>
						<key>Comment</key>
						<string>Automatic paste: read the focused field and confirm the paste.</string>
						<key>Identifier</key>
						<string>com.ethdawg.workbench</string>
						<key>IdentifierType</key>
						<string>bundleID</string>
						<key>StaticCode</key>
						<false/>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>Authorization</key>
						<string>Allow</string>
						<key>CodeRequirement</key>
						<string>identifier "com.ethdawg.workbench.preview" and anchor apple generic and certificate 1[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.2.6] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.1.13] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = GHVAAH9P5Z</string>
						<key>Comment</key>
						<string>Workbench Preview. Automatic paste: read the focused field and confirm the paste.</string>
						<key>Identifier</key>
						<string>com.ethdawg.workbench.preview</string>
						<key>IdentifierType</key>
						<string>bundleID</string>
						<key>StaticCode</key>
						<false/>
					</dict>
				</array>
				<key>PostEvent</key>
				<array>
					<dict>
						<key>Authorization</key>
						<string>Allow</string>
						<key>CodeRequirement</key>
						<string>identifier "com.ethdawg.workbench" and anchor apple generic and certificate 1[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.2.6] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.1.13] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = GHVAAH9P5Z</string>
						<key>Comment</key>
						<string>Automatic paste: send Command-V to the app the user is typing in.</string>
						<key>Identifier</key>
						<string>com.ethdawg.workbench</string>
						<key>IdentifierType</key>
						<string>bundleID</string>
						<key>StaticCode</key>
						<false/>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>Authorization</key>
						<string>Allow</string>
						<key>CodeRequirement</key>
						<string>identifier "com.ethdawg.workbench.preview" and anchor apple generic and certificate 1[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.2.6] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.1.13] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = GHVAAH9P5Z</string>
						<key>Comment</key>
						<string>Workbench Preview. Automatic paste: send Command-V to the app the user is typing in.</string>
						<key>Identifier</key>
						<string>com.ethdawg.workbench.preview</string>
						<key>IdentifierType</key>
						<string>bundleID</string>
						<key>StaticCode</key>
						<false/>
					</dict>
				</array>
				<key>ScreenCapture</key>
				<array>
					<dict>
						<key>Authorization</key>
						<string>AllowStandardUserToSetSystemService</string>
						<key>CodeRequirement</key>
						<string>identifier "com.ethdawg.workbench" and anchor apple generic and certificate 1[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.2.6] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.1.13] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = GHVAAH9P5Z</string>
						<key>Comment</key>
						<string>Snap and Snap and Talk. A profile cannot switch this on; this lets a standard user do it.</string>
						<key>Identifier</key>
						<string>com.ethdawg.workbench</string>
						<key>IdentifierType</key>
						<string>bundleID</string>
						<key>StaticCode</key>
						<false/>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>Authorization</key>
						<string>AllowStandardUserToSetSystemService</string>
						<key>CodeRequirement</key>
						<string>identifier "com.ethdawg.workbench.preview" and anchor apple generic and certificate 1[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.2.6] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.1.13] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = GHVAAH9P5Z</string>
						<key>Comment</key>
						<string>Workbench Preview. Snap and Snap and Talk. A profile cannot switch this on; this lets a standard user do it.</string>
						<key>Identifier</key>
						<string>com.ethdawg.workbench.preview</string>
						<key>IdentifierType</key>
						<string>bundleID</string>
						<key>StaticCode</key>
						<false/>
					</dict>
				</array>
				<!-- Optional. Delete this key to let macOS ask the user on first use instead. -->
				<key>SystemPolicyDesktopFolder</key>
				<array>
					<dict>
						<key>Authorization</key>
						<string>Allow</string>
						<key>CodeRequirement</key>
						<string>identifier "com.ethdawg.workbench" and anchor apple generic and certificate 1[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.2.6] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.1.13] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = GHVAAH9P5Z</string>
						<key>Comment</key>
						<string>Import Desktop screenshots into Snap History (moves the originals to the Trash).</string>
						<key>Identifier</key>
						<string>com.ethdawg.workbench</string>
						<key>IdentifierType</key>
						<string>bundleID</string>
						<key>StaticCode</key>
						<false/>
					</dict>
					<dict>
						<key>Authorization</key>
						<string>Allow</string>
						<key>CodeRequirement</key>
						<string>identifier "com.ethdawg.workbench.preview" and anchor apple generic and certificate 1[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.2.6] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[field.1.2.840.113635.100.6.1.13] /* exists */ and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = GHVAAH9P5Z</string>
						<key>Comment</key>
						<string>Workbench Preview. Import Desktop screenshots into Snap History (moves the originals to the Trash).</string>
						<key>Identifier</key>
						<string>com.ethdawg.workbench.preview</string>
						<key>IdentifierType</key>
						<string>bundleID</string>
						<key>StaticCode</key>
						<false/>
					</dict>
				</array>
			</dict>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>PayloadDescription</key>
	<string>Privacy permissions for Workbench (com.ethdawg.workbench) and Workbench Preview (com.ethdawg.workbench.preview), Developer ID team GHVAAH9P5Z. Microphone, Camera and system audio are still allowed by the user in macOS's own prompts.</string>
	<key>PayloadDisplayName</key>
	<string>Workbench privacy permissions</string>
	<key>PayloadIdentifier</key>
	<string>com.ethdawg.workbench.it.pppc</string>
	<key>PayloadOrganization</key>
	<string>REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-ORGANISATION</string>
	<key>PayloadScope</key>
	<string>System</string>
	<key>PayloadType</key>
	<string>Configuration</string>
	<key>PayloadUUID</key>
	<string>D7364E24-83EC-4756-BF97-3DA4FB5D4E9F</string>
	<key>PayloadVersion</key>
	<integer>1</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
